# pyron COSMO DISRUPTION (EX): 41236 + HOLD and RELEASE 2P/2K.
# Maintainer-reported 14z-74: this move CRASHES / resets the game.
#
# THE MOVE COSTS A METER STOCK. With an empty meter the EX pair is
# downgraded to a single button and nothing fires — the trap that cost
# three sessions on Dark Force and the Erasing Sphere. So the runner MUST
# poke the stock count ($FF8509) before the attempt, exactly as
# 72_hui_ex_es.rpl does, or this replay measures nothing:
#   POKES="1400:ff8782:11;1450:ff8782:11;1500:ff8782:11;3000:ff8509:03;3020:ff8509:03"
#
# P1 starts on the left facing right, so back = L and forward = R;
# 41236 = L -> DL -> D -> DR -> R. Then hold the two-button pair and
# release it. Two attempts (the seq dispatch can eat a frame-pinned
# input): the first with 2K (45), the second with 2P (12), so one replay
# covers both of the maintainer's reported inputs.
#
# TIMING (measured 14z-74): the match goes live ~f3000 but the round
# intro runs past it — inputs before ~f3300 do nothing. Attempts start at
# 3400 and repeat every 400 frames, the same cadence as 72_hui_ex_es.
